coder › Done. Work is on branch `env-config`.

What I changed
- `src/env.ts` (new): `fromEnv(env, prefix = 'APP_')` reads `${prefix}PORT`, `${prefix}HOST`, `${prefix}DEBUG`, `${prefix}NAME`. Absent or `''` values are skipped. Port is parsed with `Number` and must be finite, otherwise `TypeError` naming `${prefix}PORT`; debug accepts `true/1/yes` and `false/0/no` case-insensitively, otherwise `TypeError` naming `${prefix}DEBUG`; host and name stay strings.
- `src/config.ts`: added `validate(config)` — throws `TypeError` naming the field when port isn't an integer in `[1, 65535]`, or host/name is empty; otherwise returns the config.
- `src/index.ts`: `resolveConfig(file, env)` now layers `fromEnv(env)` over `merge(DEFAULTS, file)`, then validates; `env` defaults to `process.env`.
- Tests: new `src/env.test.ts` and `src/config.test.ts`, extended `src/index.test.ts`.

